Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:44:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: give one executable its own SMC checks on iOS

FEX_SMCCHECKS_FOR=<exe>=<mode> sets SMCChecks (none, mtrack or full) in
the one process whose executable base name is <exe>, compared
case-insensitively; every other process keeps the SMCChecks its
configuration gives. FEX's environment layer is its highest, so a
session-wide FEX_SMCCHECKS cannot be narrowed by an app config; this is
set over it at process start, before any code is translated. When the
variable is set, each process logs one `[smc-for]` line with its
executable and effective mode; an unknown mode is logged and ignored.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-rockstar-generated-fault.md
Offered-upstream: no; iOS crash diagnosis
---
